<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<policyDefinitionResources xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
                           revision="1.0" schemaVersion="1.0"
                           xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/GroupPolicy/2006/07/PolicyDefinitions">
  <displayName>Featherweight</displayName>
  <description>Policies for Featherweight, the light PDF reader and office suite.</description>
  <resources>
    <stringTable>
      <string id="Featherweight">Featherweight</string>
      <string id="SUPPORTED_Featherweight_4_1">Featherweight 4.1 or later</string>
      <string id="DisableUpdates">Turn off updates</string>
      <string id="DisableUpdates_Help">If you enable this policy, Featherweight never checks for updates and never updates itself, and the update options in File &gt; Options can't be changed. Its only network access is the update check, so with updates off Featherweight makes no network connections of its own.

Install new versions with the MSI or the installer instead.

If you disable or don't configure this policy, users choose in File &gt; Options whether Featherweight updates itself (on by default).</string>
      <string id="UpdateChannel">Update channel</string>
      <string id="UpdateChannel_Help">Chooses which releases Featherweight updates to.

Stable: the latest release.
Beta: the newest release, beta versions (pre-releases on GitHub) included.

If you enable this policy, users can't change the channel in File &gt; Options. If you disable or don't configure it, users choose (stable by default). This policy has no effect while "Turn off updates" is enabled.</string>
      <string id="Channel_Stable">Stable</string>
      <string id="Channel_Beta">Beta</string>
      <string id="Language">Interface language</string>
      <string id="Language_Help">Sets the language of Featherweight's menus, ribbon and dialogs.

If you enable this policy, users can't choose another language. If you disable or don't configure it, Featherweight follows Windows' display language, unless the user chooses a language in File &gt; Options.</string>
      <string id="Language_en">English</string>
      <string id="Language_nl">Dutch (Nederlands)</string>
      <string id="Language_de">German (Deutsch)</string>
      <string id="Language_fr">French (Français)</string>
      <string id="Language_es">Spanish (Español)</string>
    </stringTable>
    <presentationTable>
      <presentation id="UpdateChannel">
        <dropdownList refId="UpdateChannel" defaultItem="0">Update channel:</dropdownList>
      </presentation>
      <presentation id="Language">
        <dropdownList refId="Language" defaultItem="0">Interface language:</dropdownList>
      </presentation>
    </presentationTable>
  </resources>
</policyDefinitionResources>
